At first, while the judge of the case points out that creditors must be governed by the United States Bankruptcy Act, the New Orleans-based Fifth Circuit appeals court says the main proceeding is the commercial tender filed in Mexico.
The first point would imply ignorance of international procedural cooperation in cases of insolvency of companies with a transnational profile.
In fact, towards that end, the United Nations Model Law for the Uniformity of International Commercial Law was created, placing the American Law Institute as an arbitrator.
